{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Premise check before implementation: the central claim is FALSIFIED against the live store.\n\nAudited every REVIEW_RESULT sidecar in .tickets-tracker (3,669 events; 1,377 code_review_result_v2 + 114 v1). Across 3,673 persisted code-review findings, 3,583 (97.5%) DO carry a verification block, and every one of those blocks has exactly the keys {binary, severity_attributes}. Presence is uniform across time (v1 2026-07: 358/358; v2 2026-07: 1592/1612; v2 2026-08: 1633/1703) - not a recent fix.\n\nThe 90 findings WITHOUT a block are all legitimately unverified, not dropped:\n- 53 are tier=DET (29 advisory, 24 blocking) plus 8 with no tier - deterministic detector / fail-closed / bugfix-size-gate findings that never enter Pass-2, so no verification exists to persist.\n- 29 are tier=LLM, decision=indeterminate, reason='no-verification' - Pass-2 emitted nothing for that index and pass3_decide correctly degraded them.\n\nMechanism, for the record: review_kernel.decide.pass3_over_findings stamps verification onto every decided finding; code_review.sidecar.build_payload's _with_norm_ids is a spread ({**f, 'norm_id': ...}), so it PRESERVES every field rather than selecting a subset the way plan-review's _slim does. There is no drop site. The 'code path has no analog' assertion in the plan is incorrect - the analog is field-preservation instead of field-selection.\n\nConsequences for the plan:\n- Item 1 (persist verification blocks) is already satisfied in shipped code; nothing to implement.\n- Item 3 (round-trip backstop test) would assert behaviour that already holds - still worth adding as a regression pin, but it is not a fix.\n- Item 2 (the error signal, coverage.metrics.verification_recorded) is genuinely UNIMPLEMENTED - that identifier appears nowhere in src/, tests/, or docs/. This is the operator's stated larger concern (R3) and is the only real remaining work.\n- Item 2 as currently WORDED would misfire: 'findings lack verification while verify ran' is TRUE on any run carrying a DET-tier detector finding or an indeterminate, i.e. routinely. The signal must be scoped to LLM-tier findings excluding decision=indeterminate/reason=no-verification, or it becomes a permanent false alarm.\n\nStopping before claim/implementation: the ticket needs re-scoping to item 2 only, with a corrected detection predicate, before it is worth a plan review. The corpus the ordinal-migration work was said to be blocked on already exists (3,583 verified findings with binary + severity_attributes), so that blocker should be re-checked too."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786507742802867001,"uuid":"accba982-d1f4-44e4-a985-2d22278e2309"}